  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 42a7ef911f4c60e408989a759d2b9b18, type: 3}
  m_Name: PHP_OPERATORS
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.LessonData
  id: PHP_OPERATORS
  language: 2
  conceptTitle: Operators and Shortcuts
  symbol: += %
  relatedQuestionIds:
  - PHP_04_OPERATORS
  topics:
  - Operators
  definition: Operators are symbols that do something with values, such as adding
    them together.
  howItWorks: '+ - * / do normal maths. % (modulo) gives the remainder after division:
    10 % 4 is 2. += is a shortcut: $x += 5 means $x = $x + 5. Lines run from top
    to bottom, so each line uses the value left by the line before.'
  exampleCode: '<?php

    $apples = 9;

    $apples -= 2;

    $left = $apples %
    3;

    echo $left;

    ?>'
  exampleExplanation: '$apples -= 2 takes away 2, so $apples becomes 7. 7 % 3 is
    the remainder of 7 divided by 3: 3 goes into 7 twice (6) with 1 left over, so
    $left is 1 and echo outputs 1.'
  tip: -=, *= and /= work the same way as +=.
